# ===== Cloudflare Wrangler =====
.wrangler/
.dev.vars
# security-review-2026-05 §M1: wrangler.jsonc carries production D1 / KV
# resource IDs that must NOT be checked into the repo. The committed
# template lives at `wrangler.jsonc.example`; bootstrap a fresh checkout
# with `cp apps/cloud/api/wrangler.jsonc.example apps/cloud/api/wrangler.jsonc`
# and paste in the real IDs from `wrangler d1 create` /
# `wrangler kv namespace create`.
#
# Glob form catches macOS Finder duplicates (`wrangler 2.jsonc`,
# `wrangler 3.real-bak`, …) that the security-review-2026-05-07 §M5
# pass found accumulating in checkouts where `mv` shuffles ran. Don't
# rely on the exact-path match alone.
apps/cloud/api/wrangler.jsonc
apps/cloud/api/wrangler*.jsonc
apps/cloud/api/wrangler*.bak
apps/cloud/api/wrangler*.real-bak
# Keep the example tracked even under the glob.
!apps/cloud/api/wrangler.jsonc.example

